# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
old_db_backup/*
*.log
*.zip
resource/*
*.png
*.jpg

# The blanket *.png rule above silently excludes committed source assets too, not
# just generated/scratch ones — it was hiding src/app/icon.png (the Next.js App
# Router favicon convention) from git entirely. The file built and ran fine locally
# while being invisible to `git status`, so it would vanish on any fresh clone or CI
# checkout with no error at commit time to catch it. Exempted explicitly rather than
# narrowing the blanket rule, since it's unclear what else depends on *.png/*.jpg
# being ignored (likely course/guide thumbnails fetched into a local dev uploads/
# folder) and this only needs to unignore the one file that must ship with the repo.
!src/app/icon.png
!src/app/apple-icon.png